  "dcterms:title": "Copper-alloy ringed pin",
  "dcterms:description": "Complete polyhedral-headed ringed pin with a plain ring. The pin shaft is slightly bent towards the tip and carries faint traces of incised ornament below the head. Ringed pins of this form were the everyday cloak fastener of early medieval Ireland and the wider Norse world.",
